cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use VarDictRust in published research, please cite both the original VarDict publication (Lai et al. 2016) and this software implementation."
title: "VarDictRust: Memory-Safe, High-Performance Variant Calling for NGS"
abstract: >-
  VarDictRust is a fast, memory-safe Rust NGS variant caller for somatic and
  germline sequencing that consolidates the Java, R, and Perl VarDict pipeline
  into a single statically-compiled binary with bounded whole-genome memory.
  It delivers byte-identical output to VarDictJava v1.8.3 by default
  (--compat=vardictjava) while offering opt-in --compat=off accuracy,
  structural-variant, mate-pileup, and SAM =/X alignment fixes alongside
  --vcf-all-alleles multi-allelic VCF emission and native multithreaded BGZF,
  Tabix (.tbi), and CSI (.csi) indexing.
version: 1.0.10
date-released: "2026-11-18"
